-- title:
--   Hecke corner modules are nearly free over T^S(N)_θ
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ whose image in $\mathcal O$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space with an action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ factoring through a finite level) whose base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible. Let $S,S_{\min}$ be finite sets of naturals with every element of $S$ prime, $p\in S_{\min}\subseteq S$, such that a prime $q\neq p$ lies in $S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ (some $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $q$ acts non-trivially), and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ in the associated adic representation. Let $N,L$ be nonzero naturals with: all prime divisors of $N$ in $S$; $p^2\nmid N$; every $q\in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$ dividing $N$; $q^2\mid N$ for every prime $q\neq p$, $q\notin S_{\min}$, $q\mid N$; $q^3\nmid N$ for every prime $q\neq p$; and $L\mid N$ with $N$ and $L$ having the same prime divisors, $q^2\mid N\Rightarrow q^2\mid L$, and $L$ cube-free. Assume the weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by their integral lattice. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra $\mathbb T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two level-$N$ cusp forms generated by the operators indexed outside $S$) to $k$ such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\ell$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Write $T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) for the localisation of $\mathbb T$ at the submonoid attached to $\theta$. Finally let $M$ be an abelian group with compatible $\mathcal O$- and $T$-module structures, $B$ an $\mathcal O$-bilinear form on $M$, and assume $(M,B)$ is a corner realisation for $p,\bar\rho,N,L,S,\theta$: there are commuting Hecke and diamond operators `opFamily L ⊤ S 𝒪` on the degree-one cohomology `H1 L ⊤ 𝒪` of $\Gamma_0(L)$, a character $\bar\theta$ on the generators with $\bar\theta(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid LN$, with $\bar\theta(U_q)=0$ when $q^2\mid L$ and $\bar\theta(U_p)\neq0$ when $p\mid L$ and $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, an idempotent splitting of the $\mathcal O$-algebra generated by these operators together with a corner index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map from the corner ring to $k$ inducing $\bar\theta$, parabolicity of all classes in the corner submodule, and an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism of $M$ with that corner submodule carrying the $T_\ell$-action to `heckeT` and $B$ to the pairing `Bfam₀` (these conditions are summarised here). Then there exist $d\in\mathbb N$, a $T$-linear map $f\colon T^{d}\to M$ and a nonzero $c\in\mathcal O$ such that $f$ is injective and $c\,m$ lies in the image of $f$ for every $m\in M$; that is, $M$ contains a free $T$-module of rank $d$ whose image contains $cM$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-zero Eichler–Shimura and newform input to the modularity lifting method: at a cube-free level the localised cohomological Hecke module is free of some rank $d$ over the localised anemic Hecke algebra up to $\mathcal O$-torsion-free error, the integral form of the statement that each $\mathcal O$-eigencomponent has rank $d$. It feeds the subsequent self-adjointness, bijectivity and rank computation for corner realisations.
